      "To provide a realistic profile for a Chef earning $60,000 per year, we can look at industry standards. In many parts of the United States, $60,000 is a typical salary for a **Sous Chef** or a **line cook with several years of experience** working at a mid-range restaurant or a corporate dining facility.\n\nHere is an example profile:\n\n*   **Name:** Marcus Thorne\n*   **Age:** 32\n*   **Gender:** Male\n*   **Context:** Marcus has been working in the culinary industry for about eight years. He currently works as a Sous Chef at a popular gastropub in a major city. His salary reflects his level of responsibility, which includes managing kitchen inventory, supervising junior staff, and assisting the Executive Chef with menu development.",
